<cem:title lang="" subtitle="">Partnership Accepted</cem:title>
<cem:description lang="">This virtual learning object "Partnership Accepted" that makes part of the lesson No: 9, Getting the Client, which in turn belongs to the Pre-intermediate (B1.2) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, is intended to work on: discuss jobs and work; exchange opinions; change topics. The grammar of this LO refers to: expressions for changing topics speaking of; by the way; on that note; oh, that reminds me; but, e.g. we should have a party to celebrate the new contract; simple present, modal verbs, and tag questions to give and exchange opinions, e.g. I’m happy we got the contract; you were taken by surprise, weren't you, I must say that I was, I thought they would offer the contract to our competitor. Also, the vocabulary considers: jobs and work, e.g. partnership, extension, work hard, employees, desk; food and drink, e.g. luncheon, caterer, diet, vegans, vegetarians, high protein diet, meat, gluten-free, low-fat, low-sodium.</cem:description>
<cem:keyword lang="">
<cem:li>Exchange opinions</cem:li>
<cem:li>Eating habits</cem:li>
<cem:li>Change topics in a conversation</cem:li>
<cem:li>Expressions for changing topics</cem:li>
<cem:li>Food</cem:li>
<cem:li>Drink</cem:li>
<cem:li>Present subtle opinions</cem:li>
</cem:keyword>
