<cem:description>
<cem:recommendedUse lang="en">This digital resource can be used as an activity that allows the learner to reflect on the use of grammar of English language in different communicative contexts. The instructor can work further on activities and tasks that help learners to improve their procedural knowledge.</cem:recommendedUse>
<cem:triggerQuestion lang="en">When was the last time you succeeded at work?; What did you do to celebrate?</cem:triggerQuestion>
<cem:pedagogicalAspect lang="en">This learning object "Partnership Accepted" that is part of the lesson No: 9, Getting the Client, which in turn belongs to the Pre-intermediate (B1.2) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, allows the learner to develop the following topics: expressions for changing topics speaking of; by the way; on that note; oh, that reminds me; but, e.g. we should have a party to celebrate the new contract; simple present, modal verbs, and tag questions to give and exchange opinions, e.g. I’m happy we got the contract; you were taken by surprise, weren't you, I must say that I was, I thought they would offer the contract to our competitor. It is presented within the context of discuss jobs and work;exchange opinions; change topics. The student will be exposed to vocabulary related to: jobs and work, e.g. partnership, extension, work hard, employees, desk; food and drink, e.g. luncheon, caterer, diet, vegans, vegetarians, high protein diet, meat, gluten-free, low-fat, low-sodium. Learners will develop their language skills by using an online content as well as the guidance of a SENA instructor.</cem:pedagogicalAspect>
<cem:learningGoal lang="en">The purpose of this learning object is to use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts.</cem:learningGoal>
</cem:description>
</cem:educational>
