<cem:description lang="en">This lesson: "Getting the Client" belongs to Pre-intermediate (B1.2). It is composed of twelve learning objects, that have the following learning outcomes: identify ways of improving aspects of communication in english based on the learning outcomes for level Pre-intermediate B; use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts; present advice on solving technical problems in a work context and appropriate for the interlocutor. On the other hand, the communicative functions of this lesson are: discuss jobs and work; exchange opinions; change topics; give advice; talk about feelings and impressions; discuss experiences they have and haven’t had; discuss how to deal with problems; write about jobs and work; write about experiences they have and haven’t had; ask for clarification.</cem:description>
</cem:resource>
